# Blocker / review / failure protocol

Authoritative standard: `.ai/MASTER_WORKFLOW.md` (§9, §11, §12). Safety and honesty take
precedence over speed and task completion. Never represent unfinished or failed work as success.

## REVIEW_REQUIRED — human decision or protected action
Set when a human approval, permission, credential/secret entry, external-service action,
destructive confirmation, or a commit/push/deploy/release (not already authorized) is needed.
Standing task authority persists: routine authorized commits/pushes/integration do not
require this status or repeated approval.
1. Pause safely before the protected operation; prepare concrete reviewable results first.
2. Set `HANDOFF.md` to `REVIEW_REQUIRED`; document the exact human action required.
3. Record what was completed, what remains unchanged, whether code/config changed, and any
   uncommitted work. 4. Record the checkpoint and sync when available. 5. Continue independent
   authorized milestone work; resume only the protected operation after its requirement is met.
6. Bundle missing inputs once: exact blocked operation/target, missing access or decision,
   recommended verified destination, consequence and completed preparation. No secret values.

## BLOCKED — recoverable technical/environmental issue
1. Run only safe, scoped diagnostics; make no speculative destructive changes.
2. If unresolved, set `BLOCKED`; record the failed command, concise error evidence, and the last
   successful step. 3. Update the existing checkpoint; batch authorized publication and verify
   actual source equality. 4. Continue independent work. Retry only with new evidence, corrected
   inputs/configuration or a bounded transient policy; change the diagnosis after repeated
   identical failure instead of repeating expensive checks or access requests.

## FAILED — task or critical validation failed
1. Preserve evidence and current work; diagnose and repair the specific failure with focused
   verification. Stop unsafe/unauthorized operations, not all independent repairs.
2. Set FAILED truthfully if acceptance remains failed; state rollback status and exact next action.
3. Record the checkpoint and actual publication/sync status; unavailable mobile access does not
   stop independent work. 4. Do not claim acceptance or bypass a failed release gate.
   Diagnostic publication requires its own scope and truthful status.

Never include secrets or full sensitive logs in any of these states.
